<title>NORWAY: CBK, Storebrand see synergy effect.</title>
<headline>CBK, Storebrand see synergy effect.</headline>
<dateline>OSLO 1997-04-29</dateline>
<text>
<p>Norway's Christiania Bank og Kreditkasse ASA and Storebrand ASA said on Tuesday they saw annual synergy effects of at least 500 million crowns from merging their operations.</p>
<p>In the longer term Norway's second largest bank and largest insurance company said they had ambitions of achieving further synergy effects, an Oslo Bourse statement said.  </p>
<p>Christiania and Storebrand announced fusion plans earlier this month, saying they hoped to merge operations by the end of the year.</p>
<p>The merger, if approved by shareholders and authorities, would form the country's largest financial group and the sixth biggest in the Nordic region.</p>
<p>--Oslo newsroom +47 22 42 50 41</p>
</text>
